## Claim under pressure

SPRINT **CAP-G1** (granular net enforce):

| Slice | Path-A expectation |
|-------|--------------------|
| HttpCap | HTTP family only (`fetch`/`http_get`/…); **no** raw sockets / bind |
| TcpCap | TCP client IO (`tcp_connect`/`tcp_write`/`tcp_read`/`tcp_close`/`tls_connect`); **no** bind / sock_raw |
| UdpCap | `bind_udp` / `udp_recv` |
| BindCap | `tcp_bind` listen |
| NetCap | Legacy supersede for soft-granular ops; **required** for `sock_raw`/`raw_socket` |
| Emit messages | Prefer stating preferred kind (honesty residual if still `&NetCap` text) |
| SECRET T2 | `tcp_write` payload refuse remains dual-path (soft re-run) |

Adversarial stance: treat **any** wrong-granular check OK as **CRIT fail-open** until dual-proved deny.

