## Hunt results

### H1 — HttpCap used for raw sockets / bind  → **CRIT (pre-fix) → FIXED**

| Fixture | Pre-fix host (`bak.pre_cap_g1`) | Post-fix product |
|---------|----------------------------------|--------------------|
| `http: &HttpCap` + `tcp_bind` | **OK (fail-open)** | **rc=1** requires `&BindCap` |
| `http: &HttpCap` + `sock_raw` | **OK (fail-open)** | **rc=1** requires `&NetCap` |
| `http: &HttpCap` + `fetch` | OK | **OK** (correct allow) |

Root cause (pre-fix product): check treated **any** of Http/Tcp/Udp/Bind as satisfying **all** NetCap sealed ops (inverted granular bag).  
Source fix: `sealed_net_kind_of` returns preferred kind; `check_caps` accepts **exact preferred** or **legacy NetCap supersede** only.

### H2 — Bind without BindCap  → **CRIT (pre-fix) → FIXED**

| Fixture | Pre-fix | Post-fix |
|---------|----------|-----------|
| `tcp: &TcpCap` + `tcp_bind` | OK (fail-open) | **rc=1** requires `&BindCap` |
| `bind: &BindCap` + `tcp_bind` | (stale host inconsistent) | **OK** |
| `net: &NetCap` + `tcp_bind` | OK | **OK** (legacy supersede) |

Runtime already had `oo_cap_require_bind` on `oo_tcp_bind` (netfloor). Gap was **check** allowing wrong granular through.

### H3 — sock_raw via TcpCap  → **CRIT (pre-fix) → FIXED**

| Fixture | Pre-fix | Post-fix |
|---------|----------|-----------|
| `tcp: &TcpCap` + `sock_raw` | OK (fail-open) | **rc=1** requires `&NetCap` |
| `net: &NetCap` + `sock_raw` | OK | **OK** |

`sealed_net_kind_of(sock_raw|raw_socket) = NetCap` (no soft granular). Runtime: `oo_cap_require_net` then residual Err product.

### H4 — Emit lowers still say only `&NetCap` when TcpCap valid  → **RESIDUAL (honesty)**

`c_emit_netio.oo` / fetch lower still print `requires &NetCap first arg` for all net free names.  
Emit gate is **cap-ident form** only (`c_arg_is_cap_ident`); **type precision is check + runtime**.  
Not fail-open (wrong type still denied at check). **Not fixed this pass** (non-CRIT). Track under CAP-G1 residual / CAPS_MATRIX row text.

### H5 — Secret sinks refuse secrets on tcp_write (T2 soft re-run)  → **GREEN (post-fix host)**

| Fixture | emit-c | check | Verdict |
|---------|--------|-------|---------|
| `secret_t2_args_tcp_write_fail` | rc=1 + `ERR\tsecret\ttcp_write sink refuses SECRET token` | rc=1 same | **PASS** |
| `secret_t2_args_write_file_fail` | rc=1 + write_file refuse | — | **PASS** |
| `secret_t2_args_println_secret_fail` | rc=1 + println refuse | — | **PASS** |
| `secret_t2_args_println_concat_fail` | rc=1 | — | **PASS** |
| `secret_t2_args_println_ok_pass` | rc=0, no secret ERR | — | **PASS** |

**Note:** Pre-fix product host (04:27, any-granular era) **malloc-aborted** (rc=134) on cap+secret sinks (`tcp_write`/`write_file`/`fetch`) instead of clean refuse — host heap defect, not secret allow. Rebuilt host restores clean T2 refuse. No T2 source change required this pass.

